In article <9bh234$3gj5$1@as121.tel.hr>, Samo Puharic
<spuharic@jagor.srce.hr> wrote:

X What mean error when I backup filesystem on 2G DAT tape with command for
X example:
X 
X vdump -0 -C /usr
X 
X I receive error on begin and on end of command output:
X 
X error[13] posting event: sys.unix.fs.advfs.fset.backup.unlock
X 
X I work on AlphaServer 4100 with True64UNIX 5.1

It means the "Event Manager" daemon is not running.  This typically
happens when doing a backup in single user mode when the system has a
minimum number of processes running.

Your backup was OK.  This is not a backup error.  If this is the only
error message, then your vdump is good.

In a future version of Tru64 UNIX the message is changed to an
informational message which tells you to ignore it if you are running
in single user mode.

                                        Bob Harris


