in article 9c04ta$j4o$1@net44p.hkbu.edu.hk, Pui Ming WONG at
s11976@net2.hkbu.edu.hk wrote on 23/04/2001 12:43:

> want to start up the thirty party "Squid" reverse
> proxy server upon bootup
> Think i should create a link under
> /sbin/rc3.d like S66squid which links to
> ../init.d/squid, a shell script to start/stop the thing
> 
> But how do i know which number to use
> (as i see there are other higher number ones like S93some-process)
> or i just make up a number
> Please advice

The number of purely arbitrary and used to order execution of startup. I use
S87squid but its an ordering choice. Here is the code from /sbin/rc3 that
processes the startup files ;-
if [ -d /sbin/rc3.d ]; then
        for f in /sbin/rc3.d/S*
        do
                if [ -s $f ]; then

                        # Invoke executable startup scripts with the shell
                        # interpreter defined within each startup script.
                        # Non-executable startup scripts will be invoked
                        # with /sbin/sh by default.
                        if [ -x $f ]; then
                                $f start
                        else
                                /sbin/sh $f start
                        fi
                fi
        done
fi

As you can see it forces it to run as bourne shell if its not executable (ie
/sbin/sh) and is in the directory order as per the for f in /sbin/rc3.d/S*

    Cheers
        Mark :)



