In article <9alqhu$l5o$1@nntp9.atl.mindspring.net> "iskander" <phi@irrational.net> writes:
>I am running into a strange problem where malloc is failing after mmaping a
>number of files with a certain total size (in this case, around 5 GB). The
>resident set size, data seg size, and virtual memory size are all set to at
>least 500 MB more than the memory size around which the problem starts to
>happen. Has anybody run into similar problems before? If so, how were they
>fixed?

There are lots of reasons MALLOC could be failing.

Are you set to eager swap mode? If so, do you have enough swap space
to handle the requests? Use swapon -s to tell how much space there is.

You are getting to 5GB or so, and your settings are 0.5GB above where
you think you are. Perhaps some roundoff in allocations is happening?
Many allocations need to allocate more space than you actually ask for.

