"Brendan E. Conboy" wrote:

>     Oh there is one other thing that annoyed me about Tru64, if the NFS
> server cannot resolve the name of a client (ie. it is not in its host
> file) the client cannot mount the filesystem...

You can change this behavior by editing /sbin/init.d/nfs and removing
-i from the MOUNTOPTS="-i" line.  I believe it's on by default
for security reasons.  Btw, mountd will also use BIND to resolve
hostnames if it's configured.

