>(logged in as root equivalent), unknowingly issued a 'rm *' command from the
>root-dir. This removed all the files in '/' including genvmunix,vmunix and
>osf_root. We managed to  recreate the links and were able to generate a
>kernel file too before rebooting. But after restart, we're getting a missing
>osf_boot  mesg.
>
>What is the significance of this file and how to restore the file and or
>system.back to its original state. We do not have any system backup for this
>machine

osf_boot is the bootstrap program that reads in and starts the
vmunix kernel image. It is absolutely critical to operation of
the system; you cannot boot without it.

You'll have to find one (and it has to be one from the correct release
of the O/S) to make your system boot.

--

