This brings up one fairly telling point - you could have had Solaris on 
faster x86 for approximately the same price with hardware completely
specified by you (as much quality as desired) so long as the appropriate
drivers existed in the OS.  But if you're going to run Solaris the Blade is
still a better way to go because Solaris/Intel binaries are almost unheard
of, and in this day when you can often get only the binaries for software,
Solaris/Sparc is still the way to go.

Depending on what you're running, the Blade will outperform a 
VMS DS10 costing 3-4X as much.  For instance, see my oft mentioned
"MYBENCHMARK" "disk I/O" measurements - the URL to my last post
is a mile long and would wrap 4 times, but you can get there by going to: 

