Hello Paul,

when the system boots and tries to load NT you will probably be under 
AlphaBios. To use Tru64 you must switch to the SRM-Console. If you want 
this you have to enter the BIOS settings (press F2 while booting). Under 
CMOS-Setup yopu will find "advanced cmos setup". There you can choose which 
console should be loaded (AlphaBios, VMS, and UNIX). You have to choose 
UNIX. Then switch your PWS off and wait a few seconds. After booting again 
SRM should be loaded. Warning: it may happen that you do not see anything 
on the screen, thats because the IO might be directed to the serial port to 
use a terminal! If you are at SRM (">>>" prompt on the screen) type "help" 
and you will get a list of commands which you can use. Use boot + params to 
boot you system (Tru64 or Linux, you cannot boot NT under SRM). 
And if you have got a PWS433a you might have another problem booting Tru64:
as far as i have heard it boots on from SCSI-Disks (normally just in 433au) 
and only from a Qlogic 1040bUX controller (i might be wrong informed).

Hope I helped

Pentyern

