Well, I alsmot hesitate to mention this because threads and signals
are like oil and water ... they don't mix very well :-)

But IIRC, you could use SIGUSR1 or SIGUSR2 to wake your other thread
out of a blocking select() or recv().

Note that several of the "middleware" products , notably MQ Series,
use threads and signals themselves ... and you have to play by
their rules if you're linking those libaries into your executable.

Hope this helps.

