You could create a pipe that you use only for manually waking a thread and
have that in select/poll.

Contrary to another message posed here, the Linux threads implementation
does not use SIGUSR1, at least not 2.x versions. The LinuxThreads
implementation uses realtime signals these days. I do not know when the
transition occurred.

